Date: November 10, 2026
System: Proxmox VE host, Tailscale, macOS client
Status: Access restored; underlying cause not confirmed
Problem
I temporarily lost access to Voyager over Tailscale. Both SSH and the Proxmox web dashboard were unreachable from my MacBook, so I needed to determine whether the issue was on the server, the private network, or the client.
Investigation
Voyager's Tailscale service was running and its Tailscale address was still assigned. The MacBook appeared as offline in the Tailscale peer information, with a last-seen time of several days earlier. That pointed toward a client connectivity issue, but did not by itself explain every symptom.
Resolution and verification
I reconnected Tailscale on the MacBook and tested the connection again. SSH on port 22 and the Proxmox dashboard on port 8006 became reachable. I also tested access while the MacBook was using a phone hotspot, confirming that remote administration worked outside the home network.
Outcome
Remote access was restored without rebuilding the server or changing its management address. I did not confirm whether a separate LAN interruption or host power-management event contributed to the original failure.
Lessons learned
- Check the client and server's Tailscale status before changing firewall or server settings.
- Test individual services rather than assuming all connectivity failures share one cause.
- Verify remote access from a genuinely separate network.
- Restored access is a successful recovery, but it does not automatically establish root cause.
